			"id": "agent-analysis-rdb-preference-telemetry-pipeline",
			"interpretation": "This scope owns HMOS World's persistence and telemetry: two RDB stacks plus a preference store feeding a click/exposure pipeline. TrackManager (singleton) resets preference key APP_TRACK_DATA, builds TrackCommonData from AppStorage BUNDLE_INFO and deviceInfo, opens TrackTable, and registers UIObserver 'willClick' and 'navDestinationSwitch' listeners; reportData stamps time and inserts TrackServiceData, and a 60s interval queries all rows, wraps them in TrackModel, posts via TrackService.postTrackData, then deletes all rows on success or above 1000 buffered rows. TrackTable maps TrackServiceData to ValuesBucket with null-coalescing and back via sealData; RdbStore opens 'hmosWorldDatabase.db' (S1), creates the 13-column trackTable, runs insert/delete/query in @Concurrent taskpool tasks typed by TableTypeEnum, returning [] on query failure. Separately, database/FormRdbHelper (singleton over RdbUtils, 'database.db' S1) CRUDs FormInfoTable; PreferenceManager ('HMosWorldStoreWithNet') stores JSON-stringified values with one re-init retry and deletes keys whose JSON fails to parse; PreferenceCacheHelper layers Record sub-key get/set; MockRequest serves rawfile mock JSON. Cross-boundary: TrackServiceData/TrackModel/TrackEventType come from ../model/TrackModel.ets. Contract: keep store names, security levels, null-vs-absent bucket semantics and the sqlite_sequence reset stable; TrackService.postTrackData is a true-resolving stub whose real upload must preserve delete-only-on-success.",
